mb|1N|mb|2S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|There are two ways to play after there is interference over 1N. The best way is to play a convention called |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lebensohl,Lebensohl^*N|CP||FP||at| which is very complicated.|
n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If we played |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lebensohl,Lebensohl^*N|CP||FP||at| then North bids 3N which denies a spade stopper.|
n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|However, he has another choice playing Lebensohl because he has 4 hearts. He would bid 3@S. that is GF Stayman but denies a spade stopper. If he had a spade stopper he would bid 2N. I am forced to bid 3@C, because 2N can have many meanings. And then he would bid 3@S to bid Stayman with a spade stopper.|
PG| ***** 3 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Let's assume we are not playing |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lebensohl,Lebensohl^*N|CP||FP||at|. In that case, North just bids 3@S as |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=stayman,Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| and he says nothing about whether or not he has a spade stopper.|
PG| ***** 4 ***** |


