UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Let's use Bergen evaluation to see why West bid 4@S with "only" 14 HCP while many players who do not play Bergen evaluation might even pass 2@S. I highly recommend, if you only learn one thing about bidding, you should learn Bergen evaluation. It is by far the best way to improve your bidding.|
PG| ***** 30 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West has 14 HCP, +2 length points, -1 for dubious Jx of diamonds, and +1 for quality (3+ honor) spade suit for 16 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at|. Once a spade fit is established, West now has extra declarer addons. They are 2 points for the singleton, 1 point for the 4 card side club suit, and an addditional point for the 6th spade once EW finds a fit. The total is 20 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 31 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Very few players would consider the West hand worth 20 points. That is why Bergen evaluation is so useful because it is worth way more than the HCP indicate, especially after a fit is found. That is why 4@S was the correct bid and made it.|
PG| ***** 32 ***** |


