md|1SQHJ8DQJT942CJ652,SK76HKT94DA83CT94,ST942HAQ6D765CAK3,SAJ853H7532DKCQ87|sv|e|
mb|2D|mb|P|mb|3D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|3@D is another nice bid by North. You should rely on the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| once partner preempts. With a known 9-card fit, we should be in a 9-trick contract (e.g. the 3-level). We will see how it works out.|
PG| ***** 34 ***** |


mb|D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I disagree with the double, especially vulnerable. East has essentially 7 HCP The @DK is normally a very dubious card. I think pass is clearly best. Although, if you made me bid, I would bid 3@S. With 4 little hearts you don't really want to play in a 4-4 heart fit.|
PG| ***** 35 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|And absent the table talk, I would probably bid 4@H with the West hand. The hand has only 10 HCP but an ace and two kings. And normally, East is showing a nice opening hand by doubling 3@D particulary if vulnerable opposite a passed hand.|
PG| ***** 36 ***** |


mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 37 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|D7|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Normally you lead count in partner's suit if you have not raised. Here since North raised my 2@D, she can lead attitude because I know she can't have a doubleton and making the @D7 the correct lead.|
PG| ***** 38 ***** |


