mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I agree with pass by East. Many players, though, like to open light in 3rd seat and would open the hand 1@H. However, I am not a big fan of opening light at the 1 level in 3rd seat. |
PG| ***** 54 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I love to preempt, but opening light just makes it hard for partner to figure out whether or not you have a real opener when you are allowed to open light. I prefer to use the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule Of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| to determine whether or not I open at the 1 level in all 4 seats.|
PG| ***** 55 ***** |


mb|1D|mb|1S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|1N|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|1N is an interesting and reasonable call by North. It shows a good 7-10 or so with a spade stopper. I probably would raise diamonds and bid 3@D which is a weak bid. Admittedly North is a little strong to do that, though, I think it is the best tactic. We will see how this works out.|
PG| ***** 56 ***** |


