qx|A5|st||rh||ah|Board 5 IMPs   -   May 29, 2024|pn|hondo717,danpsych,IraCT,aspiring|
md|3SKJ62H7DA5CKQT764,S3HAKQJ95DKQT43C9,S9754HT843D9872C5,SAQT8H62DJ6CAJ832|sv|n|
mb|P|mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It is very annoying when the right hand player, as here, opens your suit. If not vulnerable against vulnerable, I could still bid 3@C as a preempt.|
PG| ***** 76 ***** |


mb|P|mb|1H|mb|P|mb|1S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|2D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now although West has a natural 2@D bid as it turns out 2@D is not natural in this sequence. It is called |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=4sf,Fourth Suit Forcing^*N|CP||FP||at|. It is completely artificial and simply establishes a game force.|
PG| ***** 77 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at||CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=4sf,(Fourth Suit Forcing)^*N|CP||FP||at| is an important convention for you to learn. For that click the blue link in parentheses.|
PG| ***** 78 ***** |


mb|P2N|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East cannot bid 2N, because 2@D does not show a diamond stopper. Over |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=4sf,Fourth Suit Forcing^*N|CP||FP||at|, East's choices are to bid:
^C2N with a diamond stopper;
^C2@H with 3 card heart support;
^COtherwise make some other reasonable bid, which is why East should bid 3@C.|
PG| ***** 79 ***** |


ub||
mb|3C|
pg| ***** 80 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West should now bid 3@H which is game forcing and there is still some chance they should be in slam. The 2@D bid established a game force.|
PG| ***** 81 ***** |


mb|3H|mb|P|mb|4H|mb|P|MB|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now West has an interesting choice. The hand looks like a bit of a misfit. So probably slam is not a good idea even if partner has 2 aces. However, just for fun, let's count West's points.|
PG| ***** 82 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The hand has 15  HCP, + 3 length points (2 for 6 card suit, 1 for 5 card suit), + 2 quality suit points for 20 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at|. Further, in this case, a fit was not really established we do not add count 2 points for each singleton and an extra point for the 4+ card diamond suit to get the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at| once a fit is established.|
PG| ***** 83 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Regardless, with 20 points not counting the addons it would not be unreasonable for West to bid RKCB. Again Bergen hand evaluation lets you evaluate your hand much mor accurately.|
PG| ***** 84 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I recommend when the hearts are trumps, you play |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback^*N|CP||FP||at| RKCB. So 4@S is the correct bid for West.|
PG| ***** 85 ***** |


mb|4S|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East has 2 key cards and not the @HQ and bids the 3rd setp which is 5@D (2 key cards, not the HQ). I suggest you adopt |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback^*N|CP||FP||at| RKCB when hearts are trump (e.g. use 4@S as RKCB).|
PG| ***** 86 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That is assuming you play the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=queenask,Queen Ask^*N|CP||FP||at| 4@S is much better as RKCB because it allows you to do the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=queenask,Queen Ask^*N|CP||FP||at| when you have 1 or 4 key cards.|
PG| ***** 87 ***** |


mb|5D|mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|MB|?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Once you bid 4@S you should bid slam if you have 5 key cards or 4 key cards and the trump queen. That is the rule you should always use when bidding RKCB. You are committed to bidding 6 with 5 key cards or 4 keys and the trump queen. Otherwise you should not bid RKCB.|
PG| ***** 88 ***** |


mb|6H|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 89 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
